10  REM PERFECT PAUL ][ SINGS YELLOW SUBMARINE
20  REM LENNON / MCCARTNEY 1966
30  REM DECTALK ARRANGEMENT FROM THE
40  REM TALKER/80 VCF WEST 2025 DISK
50  REM ---- PACING ----
60  REM EACH DATA ITEM CARRIES ITS LENGTH IN
70  REM MS. 900 LOOPS = 1 SECOND, SO MS * .9
80  REM IS REAL TIME. SENDING THE STRING
90  REM ALREADY TAKES LEN * SD, SO THAT IS
100  REM SUBTRACTED - IT IS THE BIGGER HALF
110  REM OF THE GAP. PF = .9 RUNS SLIGHTLY
120  REM AHEAD SO THE CARD'S 8 DEEP QUEUE
125  REM KEEPS IT GAPLESS. .8 IS STILL SAFE,
127  REM .7 GETS CLOSE TO FILLING THE QUEUE.
130 PF = .9: REM PACING FACTOR
140 SD = 3: REM LOOPS PER CHAR TO SEND
150 DR =  - 16192: REM SLOT 4  ($C0C0)
160  HOME 
170  PRINT "PERFECT PAUL ]["
180  PRINT "SINGS YELLOW SUBMARINE": PRINT 
190 M$ = "[:PHONE ARPA SPEAK ON]"
200  FOR L = 1 TO 23
210  READ P$,MS
220  PRINT "  PHRASE ";L;" OF 23"
230 S$ = M$ + P$: GOSUB 900
240  NEXT L
250  PRINT : PRINT "DONE."
260  END 
900  REM ---- SEND S$, THEN WAIT OUT THE
910  REM      MS IT WILL TAKE TO SPEAK,
920  REM      LESS THE TIME SPENT SENDING
930  FOR I = 1 TO  LEN (S$): POKE DR, ASC ( MID$ (S$,I,1)): NEXT I
940  POKE DR,13
950 WT = MS * .9 * PF -  LEN (S$) * SD
960  IF WT > 0 THEN  FOR W = 1 TO WT: NEXT W
970  RETURN 
